# ^ The mistboard-engine commit the prod build checks out (railpack build step).
# Belief-update fail-safe + telemetry (2026-08-23): 91e73d6 makes the worker
# project each belief update's cost (per-world EWMA learned per host) BEFORE
# starting it and refuse the turn with an explicit BeliefUpdateOverBudget error
# when it cannot fit the wall deadline (fail closed — no fallback move; issue
# #11, game 12c8ff99: the update ran 20s+ inside the old ~22s watchdog and the
# seat was forfeited silently). Also persists the update cost (feed.obsMs,
# max |P|, learned rates) in the per-move diagnostics next to componentMs, and
# alerts on stderr for projection refusals + past-deadline responses. Pairs
# with the web-side watchdog decoupling (fow-engine-budget.ts: liveness bound
# only, 60s cap) — with the raised deadline the projection refuses only truly
# unservable turns. Kill switch: FOW_WORKER_OBS_PROJECTION=0.
# Rollback target: 350dc20 (v1.6 ship; drops the projection + telemetry only,
# no registry or env changes).
#
# Misty v1.6 (2026-08-23): 350dc20 ships the frozen v1.6 profile (v1.5 + the
# catastrophe prune's net-hang floor, hv_prune_net_floor=300) + worker id
# python-v2-v1.6. Fixes the Qxe8/Qxf2 net-hang class (games 42b652b6 move 24,
# 12c8ff99 move 30 — the second prod instance triggered the ship). The ref also
# carries the 2026-08-22 open-source-release engineering (variant guards moved
# behind the variant-hooks registry, dead-flag collapse, analysis module) — all
# validated byte-identical by the parity + golden-trace suites (1,327 green).
# Rollback target: e97009e (drops v1.6 + today's refactors; registry keeps
# v1.6 KNOWN-only until the Phase-2 offer flip, so rollback needs no registry
# change if done before that flip).
# Decision timing telemetry (2026-08-13): e97009e forwards `componentMs`
# (sf_eval / sf_children / eq_pass / select_leaf / kluss / expand_seed),
# `searchSeconds`, and `treeNodes` from gt_cfr into the live decision's
# diagnostics, which the platform already writes into the live-engine-decision
# artifact (readable since #287). think_time_ms minus searchSeconds is the
# UNBUDGETED remainder — belief enumeration + transport — i.e. the ~5s floor in
# #283, measured directly instead of inferred from clock deltas. Telemetry only:
# no move-path, budget, or protocol change, and the diagnostics builder is
# best-effort (returns {} on any error), so a regression here cannot alter play.
# Rollback target: 1bca757 (the previous pin; drops the three fields, nothing
# else). No registry or env changes either way.
#
# Worker budget fields (2026-07-30): 1bca757 makes the worker read `workerDeadlineMs`
# for its wall deadline and `computeBudgetMs` for the compute cap, instead of taking
# both from the single `watchdogTimeoutMs` key that carried the COMPUTE budget. The
# usable pick window is that value minus ~1450ms of guards, vetoed below 3000ms, so
# any compute budget under ~4450ms sent EVERY move to an unsearched deadline-guard —
# at 3+2, any clock below ~29.8s. Prod game 8d08b93a ended at 32.6s, 233ms from the
# cliff. Paired with the web-side payload split (engine-service.ts
# engineTurnPoolPayload), which still sends the legacy key so either side can deploy
# first. Also carries cbe24d1 (jungle repetition context in UCI search), which was on
# engine main but had not yet been deployed.
# Rollback target: cc959fb (the previous pin; drops both of the above, no registry or
# env changes needed since the legacy key is still sent).
